.TH REPO "1" "October 2026" "repo config" "Repo Manual"
.SH NAME
repo \- repo config - manual page for repo config
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B repo
\fI\,config \/\fR[\fI\,--type=<type>\/\fR] [\fI\,-z\/\fR] \fI\,get <name>\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Summary
.PP
Read and write per\-user repo settings
.PP
repo config [\-\-type=<type>] set <name> <value>
repo config unset <name>
repo config [\-z] list
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show this help message and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-type\fR=\fI\,TYPE\/\fR
validate and canonicalize the value as this type for get and set (bool, int)
.TP
\fB\-z\fR, \fB\-\-null\fR
terminate output of get and list with NUL instead of newline, and separate key and value with a newline
.SS Logging options:
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
show all output
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
only show errors
.SS Multi\-manifest options:
.TP
\fB\-\-outer\-manifest\fR
operate starting at the outermost manifest
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-outer\-manifest\fR
do not operate on outer manifests
.TP
\fB\-\-this\-manifest\-only\fR
only operate on this (sub)manifest
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-this\-manifest\-only\fR, \fB\-\-all\-manifests\fR
operate on this manifest and its submanifests
.PP
Run `repo help config` to view the detailed manual.
.SH DETAILS
.PP
The 'repo config' command reads and writes repo's own per\-user settings. These
are separate from git's config and from a checkout's settings; see
docs/repoconfig.md for where they live and which settings repo understands.
.PP
Settings are named <section>.<name>, e.g. sync.smartsync. 'get' prints every
value of the setting and exits 1 without output if it is not set, like `git
config`.
.PP
Values are stored as strings. With \fB\-\-type\fR, 'set' validates the value and stores
it in canonical form (e.g. "on" as "true", "1k" as "1024"), and 'get' prints the
canonical form, like `git config \fB\-\-type\fR`.
